From bf82c200bfb31353dcc3ae2786bc8cb664dc9286 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manikanta Pubbisetty <mpubbise@codeaurora.org>
Date: Fri, 2 Aug 2019 10:41:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ath11k: enable pn offload

Enabling PN checking in the hardware; i.e, the hardware checks
the PN of the received packets and report the error to
the host for further handling. PN errors will be reported via
WBM rx release ring and the default action is to drop the
packet with PN error.

The following command can be used to check for PN errors;
"cat /sys/kernel/debug/ath11k/soc_rx_stats | grep -i pn"

Sample Output:
PN check fail: 210
PN err: 0

Signed-off-by: Manikanta Pubbisetty <mpubbise@codeaurora.org>
